# Hosting and database

- Production is Hostinger at https://giftingstore.online. Do not treat Vercel as the deploy target.
- Company portals are `https://{portal_slug}.giftingstore.online`. Each portal host is a **Hostinger parked domain (alias)** on `giftingstore.online`. Regular Hostinger "subdomains" do **not** reach the Node app — never create those via API.
- `ROOT_DOMAIN=giftingstore.online` belongs in the Hostinger env. Parked hosts get their own DNS/SSL; wildcards alone are not enough for HTTPS.
- Provisioning uses `HOSTINGER_API_TOKEN`, `HOSTINGER_ACCOUNT_USERNAME`, `HOSTINGER_WEBSITE_DOMAIN`, and `CRON_SECRET` (server-only). Never commit tokens.
- This app's Supabase project is `ajysowosgjaipczrwpfv` (`corporate-gifting-crm`, ap-south-1) in org `smoddqkpbnbvcqjujvmu`. Ignore `robust-gifting-crm` and `vilms-saas-local-dev` on the same account.
- Never apply SQL to Supabase (no apply_migration/execute_sql) and never ask to; deliver migration + rollback files under `supabase/migrations` and `supabase/rollbacks`.
- Never call the live Hostinger API; use `HOSTINGER_MOCK=1` locally.
